  "definition": "Multimodal AI refers to artificial intelligence systems that process, fuse, and generate content across multiple data modalities\u2014including text, images, audio, video, and 3D\u2014within a unified model architecture. Multimodal systems learn cross-modal alignments through joint embedding spaces, enabling capabilities such as image captioning, visual question answering, text-to-image synthesis, and real-time audio-visual understanding that single-modality models cannot achieve.",
